{title: America The Beautiful}
{key: G}

{comment: Verse 1}
O [G]beautiful for [D]spacious skies,
For [D7]amber waves of [G]grain
For purple mountain [D]majesties,
A[A]bove the [A7]fruited [D]plain![D7]
A[G]merica! A[D]merica!
God [D7]shed his grace on [G]thee
And [C]crown thy good with [G]brotherhood,
From [C]sea to [D7]shining [G]sea!

{comment: Verse 2}
O [G]beautiful for [D]pilgrim feet,
Whose [D7]stern impassioned [G]stress
A thoroughfare of [D]freedom beat,
A[A]cross the [A7]wilder[D]ness![D7]
A[G]merica! A[D]merica!
God [D7]mend thine every [G]flaw
Con[C]firm thy soul in [G]self-control,
Thy [C]liber[D7]ty in [G]law!

{comment: Verse 3}
O [G]beautiful for [D]heroes proved,
In [D7]liberating [G]strife.
Who more than self their [D]country loved,
And [A]mercy [A7]more than [D]life![D7]
A[G]merica! A[D]merica!
May [D7]God thy gold re[G]fine
Till [C]all success be [G]nobleness,
And [C]every [D7]gain di[G]vine!

{comment: Verse 4}
O [G]beautiful for [D]patriot dream,
That [D7]sees beyond the [G]years
Thine alabaster [D]cities gleam,
Un[A]dimmed by [A7]human [D]tears![D7]
A[G]merica! A[D]merica!
God [D7]shed his grace on [G]thee
And [C]crown thy good with [G]brotherhood,
From [C]sea to [D7]shining [G]sea!

{comment: Verse 5}
O [G]beautiful for [D]halcyon skies,
For [D7]amber waves of [G]grain,
For purple mountain [D]majesties
A[A]bove the e[A7]nameled [D]plain![D7]
A[G]merica! A[D]merica!
God [D7]shed his grace on [G]thee
Till [C]souls wax fair as [G]earth and air
And [C]music-[D7]hearted [G]sea!

{comment: Verse 6}
O [G]beautiful for [D]pilgrims feet,
Whose [D7]stem impassioned [G]stress
A thoroughfare for [D]freedom beat
A[A]cross the [A7]wilder[D]ness![D7]
A[G]merica! A[D]merica!
God [D7]shed his grace on [G]thee
Till [C]paths be wrought through [G]wilds of thought
By [C]pilgrim [D7]foot and [G]knee!

{comment: Verse 7}
O [G]beautiful for [D]glory-tale
Of [D7]liberating [G]strife
When once and twice, for [D]man's avail
Men [A]lavished [A7]precious [D]life![D7]
A[G]merica! A[D]merica!
God [D7]shed his grace on [G]thee
Till [C]selfish gain no [G]longer stain
The [C]banner [D7]of the [G]free!

{comment: Verse 8}
O [G]beautiful for [D]patriot dream
That [D7]sees beyond the [G]years
Thine alabaster [D]cities gleam
Un[A]dimmed by [A7]human [D]tears![D7]
A[G]merica! A[D]merica!
God [D7]shed his grace on [G]thee
Till [C]nobler men keep [G]once again
Thy [C]whiter [D7]jubi- [G]lee!
